copyright holders, in source code or object code form, and any
modified version of it that retains this exception.

"Plugin API" means the public interface that ConsolX provides for
plugins, consisting of:

  a) the types, interfaces and constants published in the
     @consolx/plugin-api package; and

  b) the messages exchanged between ConsolX and its plugin host, as
     described in the official ConsolX plugin documentation.

Internal modules of ConsolX, private communication channels between
its processes, and the API exposed to the rendering process by the
preload script are not part of the Plugin API.

"Plugin" means a work designed to be loaded and run by the ConsolX
plugin host, or declared through a ConsolX plugin manifest, that
interacts with ConsolX exclusively through the Plugin API. Themes,
terminal color schemes and other resources contributed through a
plugin manifest are Plugins.

"ConsolX Core Code" means any part of ConsolX other than the
@consolx/plugin-api package.


